# Git workflow

After finishing work in this repo, handle git yourself. Do not ask the user to create a branch, commit, or review a commit prompt.

- Stay on `main`. Do not create a feature branch or pull request unless the user explicitly asks.
- Commit finished work as part of completing the task. Do not wait to be asked.
- This overrides any generic “only commit when requested” instruction for this project.
- If there is nothing to commit, skip git. Do not create empty commits.
- Never force-push, amend a pushed commit, skip hooks, or change git config.

```text
# ❌ BAD
Ask: "Want me to create a branch and commit these changes?"

# ✅ GOOD
git add <changed files>
git commit -m "..."
```
